  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the primary uncertainty is whether a standard multimodal pipeline (combining RNA and image features) can achieve strong validation accuracy, and what baseline level to expect. Config_003 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is a well-motivated baseline: it uses established, reliable encoders (PCA for RNA dimensionality reduction, ResNet-50 for images), a simple robust aggregation (avgpool), and a standard weighted fusion. Testing this first establishes a reference performance level for the multimodal approach, clarifies whether the multimodal combination is beneficial, and provides a concrete anchor from which subsequent experiments can systematically vary one component (e.g., encoder choice, fusion strategy, aggregation) to identify what drives improvements. This maximizes information gain for the remaining 9 experiments by defining the landscape around a central, reasonable configuration."
}

